@startuml egress
' Hand-maintained. Source of truth = the allowed-endpoints default of each leaf workflow.
' Regenerate the lists with: grep -A20 "allowed-endpoints:" .github/workflows/*.yml
title Egress allowlists — harden-runner policy per phase, both trees (default "block")

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

package "core — in every configurable phase of BOTH trees" as CORE #FFFFFF {
  [github.com:443]
  [api.github.com:443]
  [objects.githubusercontent.com:443]
  [release-assets.githubusercontent.com:443]
  [github-releases.githubusercontent.com:443]
}

package "java build / test phase\njava-build · java-lint · java-unit · java-integration · java-dependency-graph" as P1 #E8F0FE {
  [repo.maven.apache.org:443] as M1
  [repo1.maven.org:443] as M2
  [repo.spring.io:443] as M3
  [repository.jboss.org:443] as M4
}

package "security phase\njava-security.yml" as P2 #E6F4EA {
  [maven: apache · spring · jboss] as S_MVN <<no repo1.maven.org>>
  [ghcr.io + pkg-containers] as S_GHCR
  [uploads.github.com:443] as S_UP <<SARIF upload>>
  [raw.githubusercontent.com:443] as S_RAW
  [check.trivy.dev · get.trivy.dev] as S_TRIVY
  [get.anchore.io:443] as S_ANCHORE
  [mirror.gcr.io:443] as S_GCR
  [timestamp.sigstore.dev:443] as S_TS
}

package "docker phase\njava-docker.yml" as P3 #FEF7E0 {
  [maven: apache · repo1] as D_MVN <<no spring / jboss>>
  [auth.docker.io · registry-1.docker.io\nproduction.cloudfront.docker.com] as D_DH <<buildpack pulls>>
  [mirror.gcr.io:443] as D_GCR
  [ghcr.io + pkg-containers] as D_GHCR
  [toolbox-data.anchore.io:443] as D_ANCHORE <<Syft>>
  [raw.githubusercontent.com:443] as D_RAW
  [fulcio · rekor · tuf-repo-cdn · timestamp\n.sigstore.dev] as D_SIG
}

package "gitops phase\ndeploy-gitops.yml" as P4 #FCE8E6 {
  [ghcr.io + pkg-containers] as G_GHCR
  [fulcio · rekor · tuf-repo-cdn · timestamp\n.sigstore.dev] as G_SIG <<cosign verify>>
}

package "python phases — same shape, different upstreams" as PY #E3F2FD {
  [pypi.org:443] as PY_PYPI
  [files.pythonhosted.org:443] as PY_PH
  [raw.githubusercontent.com:443] as PY_RAW <<setup-python version manifest>>
  [index.docker.io + auth · registry-1\nproduction.cloudfront.docker.com] as PY_DH <<docker phase: pack pulls the builder>>
  [deps.paketo.io:443] as PY_PAKETO <<docker phase · REASONED, NOT OBSERVED>>
}

package "hardcoded — no input, always block" as P5 #EEEEEE {
  [tag.yml] as T <<github.com · api.github.com>>
  [auto-release.yml] as AR <<+ uploads.github.com>>
  [workflow-lint.yml] as WL <<+ ghcr.io for zizmor>>
  [build-gate] as BG <<block, no allowlist>>
}

CORE --> P1
CORE --> P2
CORE --> P3
CORE --> P4
CORE --> PY

P1 -[hidden]- P2
P2 -[hidden]- P3
P3 -[hidden]- P4
P4 -[hidden]- PY

note bottom of CORE
  Every job: egress-policy (default "block")
  + disable-sudo: true. The consumer appends
  hosts via extra-*-endpoints; the base list
  above always stays intact.
end note

note right of P3
  Buildpack builds reach a broad set of
  registries — this is the phase most likely
  to need extra-docker-endpoints. Denied hosts
  show up in the harden-runner run summary;
  watch the first run after a change instead
  of guessing.
end note

note right of P2
  ⚠️ The lists are NOT symmetrical: security
  omits repo1.maven.org, docker omits
  repo.spring.io / repository.jboss.org.
  Each is trimmed to what that phase observed
  — copying a list wholesale re-widens it.
end note

note right of PY
  The python leaves drop every Maven host
  (apache · repo1 · spring · jboss) and add the
  PyPI pair instead. Sigstore, Trivy, Syft,
  GHCR and mirror.gcr.io are identical to the
  java docker/gitops phases — deploy-gitops.yml
  is literally the same file.

  ⚠️ deps.paketo.io was reasoned about, not read
  out of a run summary. Confirm it against the
  first audit-policy run and drop it if the
  buildpack never reaches it.
end note

footer docs/egress.puml — Bigorno12/ci-cd-templates
@enduml
